  "facts": [
    "Ovit Tunnel, Turkey's second‑longest highway tunnel, stretches 14,346 meters in twin tubes, including a 1,369‑meter avalanche cut‑and‑cover section, making it the world’s seventh longest road tunnel.",
    "Groundbreaking for Ovit Tunnel occurred on 12 May 2012 with Prime Minister Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, and the tunnel finally opened to traffic on 13 June 2018, three years behind its original 2015 target.",
    "Designed to bypass Mount Ovit’s 2,640‑meter pass, the tunnel connects İkizdere in Rize Province to İspir in Erzurum Province, linking Eastern Anatolia directly to the Black Sea coast."
